.venv-report/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# New campaign (2026-08-15, see campaign/PLAN.md): tracing is off
# (fresh_server_replay.py --no-trace-proposals) so run dirs are ~25KB, not
# the ~1-1.5MB/run they'd be with proposals.jsonl -- but still not tracked in
# git (root disk sits at 96% full; git blobs are a real, avoidable cost, and
# these runs are regeneratable from the campaign scripts + prompts). Old,
# already-tracked runs under old_runs/ are untouched by this rule.
runs/**

# macOS / Slurm output noise
.DS_Store
casc-*.out
setup_nibi.log
after_build.log

# SPEED-Bench prompt texts (addendum step 7): NVIDIA Evaluation Dataset License + third-party sources
# (HLE asks that its questions stay off the open web); this repo is public. Rebuild with
# scripts/build_speedbench_prompts.py and check against campaign/addendum/speedbench/cases.csv.
prompts/speedbench/
prompts/speedbench_qwen3/

# autoresearch/ (2026-09-02, see autoresearch/README.md): per-iteration
# scratch -- the guard arm's run dirs are rewritten every loop iteration,
# and metrics.json/baseline.json are machine-specific GPU output. Only
# autoresearch/results.tsv (the durable experiment log) and the code /
# program.md are tracked.
autoresearch/runs/
autoresearch/logs/
autoresearch/metrics.json
autoresearch/baseline.json
autoresearch/cross_method_runs/
autoresearch/cross_method_logs/

